.\" ###### Setup ############################################################
.Dd November 26, 2026
.Dt System\-Maintenance 1
.Os System\-Maintenance
.\" ###### Name #############################################################
.Sh NAME
.Nm System\-Maintenance
.Nd performs system maintenance tasks
.\" ###### Synopsis #########################################################
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm System\-Maintenance
.Op Fl k | Fl \-interactive\-kernel\-removal
.Nm System\-Maintenance
.Op Fl h | Fl \-help
.Nm System\-Maintenance
.Op Fl v | Fl \-version
.\" ###### Description ######################################################
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm System\-Maintenance
runs automated system maintenance tasks to keep an operating system installation clean and up to date.
Executing maintenance tasks requires superuser (root) privileges.
These tasks include:
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
Updating package repository indices
.It
Repairing interrupted package configurations and missing dependencies
.It
Installing all available system package updates
.It
Auto\-removing unused dependencies, purging residual configurations, and cleaning package caches
.It
Removing obsolete kernel packages (on Debian/Ubuntu systems)
.It
Refreshing Snap packages and installing device firmware updates, if supported
.It
Updating file, GeoIP, and package search caches
.It
Synchronising the system clock via NTP and updating the hardware clock
.It
Trimming SSD filesystems and ZFS storage pools
.It
Running custom package\-version filter scripts from
.Pa /etc/system\-maintenance.d/
.El
.\" ###### Arguments ########################################################
.Sh ARGUMENTS
The following options are available:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl k | Fl \-interactive\-kernel\-removal
Prompts interactively before removing obsolete kernel packages (applicable on Debian/Ubuntu systems).
.It Fl h | Fl \-help
Prints the program's command\-line parameters and exits.
.It Fl v | Fl \-version
Prints the program version and exits.
.El
.\" ###### Files ############################################################
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Pa /etc/system\-maintenance.d/[0\-9][0\-9]*
Optional filter scripts executed at the end of maintenance with the path to a temporary file listing installed packages and versions.
.El
.\" ###### Exit status ######################################################
.Sh EXIT STATUS
The
.Nm
tool exits with 0 on success, and >0 in case of an error.
.\" ###### Examples #########################################################
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bl -bullet
.It
sudo System\-Maintenance
.It
sudo System\-Maintenance \-\-interactive\-kernel\-removal
.It
sudo System\-Maintenance \-k
.It
System\-Maintenance \-\-help
.It
System\-Maintenance \-h
.It
System\-Maintenance \-\-version
.It
System\-Maintenance \-v
.El
